<div class="space-y-5">
  <div>
    <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Auto-Reply Rules</h4>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">Automatically send predefined responses when incoming messages match certain conditions. Ensures customers get immediate replies even when no agent is available.</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Trigger Types</h5>
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-800">Keyword</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-blue-700 mt-1">Triggers when an incoming message contains the specified keyword. Case-insensitive. Example: keyword "hello" matches "Hello!", "Say hello", etc.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-purple-200 bg-purple-50 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-purple-800">First Message</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-purple-700 mt-1">Triggers only when a contact sends their very first message (no prior outgoing messages exist). Ideal for welcome messages.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-orange-200 bg-orange-50 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-orange-800">Outside Hours</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-orange-700 mt-1">Triggers when a message is received outside business hours (before 9 AM or after 6 PM). Use for out-of-office responses.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">How It Works</h5>
    <ul class="text-xs text-gray-600 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
      <li>When a text message arrives, the system checks all <strong>active</strong> rules: keywords first, then first-message, then outside-hours</li>
      <li>The <strong>first matching rule</strong> triggers a reply — only one auto-reply per incoming message</li>
      <li>The reply is sent via the WhatsApp API and appears in the chat like any other outgoing message</li>
      <li>Auto-replies only work for text messages (not media, reactions, or button replies)</li>
      <li>You can activate/deactivate rules at any time without deleting them</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Rules & Limits</h5>
    <ul class="text-xs text-gray-600 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
      <li><strong>Name</strong> and <strong>Reply Body</strong> are required</li>
      <li><strong>Keyword</strong> is required when trigger type is "Keyword"</li>
      <li>Multiple keyword rules can exist; the first match wins</li>
      <li>Only one "First Message" and one "Outside Hours" rule is typically needed</li>
      <li>Auto-replies count toward your WhatsApp API message quota</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2">Common Errors</h5>
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-red-50 border border-red-100 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">"Name can't be blank"</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-red-600 mt-1">Every rule needs a descriptive name to identify it in the list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-red-50 border border-red-100 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">"Keyword can't be blank"</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-red-600 mt-1">When using the "Keyword" trigger type, you must specify the keyword. Switch to a different trigger type if not needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-red-50 border border-red-100 p-3">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-red-800">"Reply body can't be blank"</p>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-red-600 mt-1">The auto-reply message cannot be empty. Enter the response text to be sent automatically.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
